> does/should this also address #72320? the symptom (cannot evict pod that is not actually contributing to the "ready pods" count) sounds very similar

@liggitt I only accounted for the 'pending' pod phase.  CrashLoopBackoff is not a phase.  For that case, I definitely think we would want to ensure there are enough healthy replicas before removing.  In particular, the pod may have already been 'Ready' and previously counted in the PDB calculations, and there may be a delete operation going on elsewhere of another pod when this one fails.  The CrashLoopBackoff pod might still have good data, and the condition might be temporary (eg, dns failure of some needed resource, application exits 1), and it might be bad to remove it without ensure there are enough healthy replicas.

That would probably be best solved with my other patch (modified for crashloopbackoff instead of pending) in conjunction with this patch.
